---
description: Enforces the Travel Agency demo static-site folder and layering conventions.
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the demo project structure strictly (static site — no Node/Express/Next unless later explicitly approved):

Site root (HTML pages mirroring demo URLs):
- `/` → `index.html`
- Page directories matching sitemap URLs (e.g. `destinations/`, `tours/`, `car-rental/`, `plan-your-trip/`, `travel-guides/`, `gallery/`, `about/`, `contact/`)
- Detail pages under their section with slug folders or HTML files as established in the repo

Shared assets & code:
- `css/` → Global and page styles (design tokens / design system first)
- `js/` → Progressive-enhancement scripts only (e.g. `main.js`, trip planner logic)
- `assets/images/`, `assets/icons/` → Static media
- `data/` → Illustrative content (destinations, packages, vehicles, guides, testimonials, etc.)

Documentation:
- `docs/` → Product, SEO, architecture-vs-demo, visual style, implementation epics

Do not:
- Scaffold `backend/`, `frontend/` Next apps, CMS, auth, or payment systems for the demo
- Mix production-ops screens into the customer demo unless separately approved
- Introduce new folder conventions without verifying existing ones
- Break naming conventions already established in the repo
